<section class="band" aria-labelledby="lp-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Landing page</span>
      <h2 id="lp-h">One page, one trail, six stops</h2>
      <p class="lede">Each section is a waypoint on the gutter trail. Each one gets a single orchestrated animation, with nothing else moving on it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="lmap">
      <div class="lrow"><div><h3>Hero</h3><div class="anim">Point cloud assembles, route draws</div></div><p>Headline, the live scan canvas, "Try it on your phone" QR, and Log in / Sign up in the nav. React Three Fiber renders the real scan here.</p></div>
      <div class="lrow"><div><h3>The problem</h3><div class="anim">Sticky scroll: flat map turns 3D</div></div><p>A cluttered 2D floor plan pinned on screen tilts into the 3D scan as you scroll. One stat counts up (Magic UI Number Ticker), for example how long it took a first-timer to find the hardware lab. Use a number you measured this weekend.</p></div>
      <div class="lrow"><div><h3>Our product</h3><div class="anim">Three feature panels slide in on the trail</div></div><p>Scan, share with Public / Unlisted / Private, and navigate with landmark cues. Use real screenshots from the app, not illustrations.</p></div>
      <div class="lrow"><div><h3>How to use</h3><div class="anim">Footprints step between 3 stops</div></div><p>Scan with a LiDAR iPhone, then place waypoints and approve Gemini's suggestions, then share the QR code. This is a real sequence, so the numbers mean something here.</p></div>
      <div class="lrow"><div><h3>Creators</h3><div class="anim">Flip cards, staggered entrance</div></div><p>Four cards with photo, role and links. Add a team photo caption for Devpost.</p></div>
      <div class="lrow"><div><h3>Join us</h3><div class="anim">Trail ends at a pin</div></div><p>The footprints end at a destination pin next to the CTA and a big QR code. "Map your first space."</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" id="stack" aria-labelledby="st-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Stack &amp; open-source picks</span>
      <h2 id="st-h">Borrow everything that isn't the product</h2>
      <p class="lede">Vite, React, TypeScript, Tailwind v4 and React Router. It builds to static files, so it deploys wherever your teammate picks, and Three.js stays client-side with no SSR friction.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="overflow-x:auto">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Pick</th><th>What it gives you</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>3D viewer</td><td><b>three</b> + <b>@react-three/fiber</b> + <b>@react-three/drei</b></td><td>PLYLoader for the scan, CameraControls for orbit and fly-to, Line for the route, Html for labels pinned in 3D.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Scroll story &amp; trail</td><td><b>gsap</b> + <b>@gsap/react</b></td><td>ScrollTrigger, MotionPath, DrawSVG and SplitText. Every plugin has been free since 2025.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>UI motion</td><td><b>motion</b> (formerly Framer Motion)</td><td>Layout transitions, AnimatePresence for sheets and cue cards, spring flips.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Smooth scroll</td><td><b>lenis</b></td><td>Buttery landing scroll on laptops. Leave it off in the app and under reduced motion.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>App components</td><td><b>shadcn/ui</b> (Radix)</td><td>Accessible dialog, switch, toggle group for visibility, tabs, dropdown. You own the code.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Bottom sheet</td><td><b>vaul</b></td><td>Native-feeling draggable drawer for "Where to?" on iPhone.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Toasts · QR · icons</td><td><b>sonner</b> · <b>qrcode.react</b> · <b>lucide-react</b></td><td>"Link copied", event QR codes, consistent icons.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Showpieces</td><td>Magic UI · Aceternity UI · React Bits</td><td>Copy-paste snippets. Use two or three at most (Number Ticker, Tracing Beam), restyled. Judges have seen the defaults many times.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" id="plan" aria-labelledby="pl-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Build order for Arielle</span>
      <h2 id="pl-h">What ships, what fakes well, what gets cut</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="tiers">
